fish stocks in the Baltic Sea will be on  the table of EU ministers responsible  for fisheries when they meet in  Luxembourg on april 20 they will discuss  a multi annual plan for cod herring and  Sprott to make sure that the fish stocks  in the Baltic are exploited in a  sustainable way agriculture ministers  will be briefed by the European  Commission on the mandatory country of  origin indication for food products such  as milk dairy certain types of meat and  unprocessed food this has gained  importance in the beginning of 2013 when  fraudulent use of horse meat was  detected in some processed food the  European Commission will also present a  model guarantee instrument for  agriculture prepared in cooperation with  the european investment bank this  instrument will help ease access to  finance for farmers and unlock  much-needed investment in rural areas  finally ministers will determine the e  use position at the United Nations forum  on forests taking place in May the forum  intends to strengthen long-term  international political commitments in  favor of sustainable forestry a key  element in the fight against climate  change
 

